  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAPRIGHTS- &apos;Reclaiming our Future&apos; Proje</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center for the Advancement &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Projection of the Rights of Vulnerable People (CAPRIGHTS) is a former empowerment grantee of Voice. Previous project established a safe space (Voices of Freedom Platform) in 2 secondary schools in Lagos State, where young peopleengage to explore issues around sexual violence, menstrual cycle, early &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; unwanted pregnancy &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; bullying at school. The platforms created a feedback mechanism for the students, parents &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; teachers to share their thoughts on the issues and changes takingplace amongst the participating students. A lot of feedback came from mothers of the young girls who participated in the project, as they express desire to be included in learning more about sexual &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; reproductive health rights. This desire gave rise for current project titled- &#x2018;Project Reclaim Our Lives&#x2019;

 &#x2018;Project Reclaim Our future&#x2019; is a powerful statement inspired by the desire of Ikotun Community women to take back what is left of their lives, look into the future with positivism and explore new ways of living. The overall goal of the project is to empower Ikotun women with knowledge, courage, and tools to take charge of their lives andlive life to the fullest. Key objectives and the activities they believe would help them achieve these objectivesare as follows:
&#x2022;Empowerment with adequate knowledge to make informed decisions on how many children they want and when to do so.
&#x2022;Build confidence tounderstand that they are beyond the violence they experience at home; understand what sexual violenceentails, what to do in such situation &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; where to get help
&#x2022;Facilitate cooperation for economic empowerment and emotional support through a village Saving Loan Association (VSLA) &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; safe space for men &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; women

The Change that the Project want to accomplishare at both individualand community level:
-Inspire them to learn more about their bodies and how they can make better decisions on their reproductive rights.
Financial independence- they hope that the VSLA scheme will help strengthen their savingspractices and promote alternative credit facility framework for them as they&apos;ve seen this benefit other communities where the VSLA scheme works
-Safe Space- they believethat the safe space created under the project will encourage them to open up &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; speak outabout domestic violence &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; leverage on support system within the space, to get by.
-Generally, they believe that as this project is changing their individual lives,their children and spouses can also feel the impact thereby creating a wholesome change within the entire community.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centre for the Advancement &amp; Protec</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centre for the Advancement and Protection of the Rights of Vulnerable Persons (here referred to as CAPRIGHTS-VP) is an organisationborne out of the passion and concern of 4 Nigerian professionals for the cause of the vulnerable people particularly, women, children, orphans, people with disability, the elderly, the youths (especially those who needs guidance in life) and generally the less privileged in our society.

Their vision is a just and fair society where everyone is treated equally, respected and supported to livetheir lives in fullness irrespective of the circumstances of their lives/situation they find themselves in. Their core values are -Equality; Integrity; Mutual Respect; Accountability; and Transparency.

CAPRIGHTS-VP focuses on education, counseling, legal support, economic empowerment, transformative change etc. for the vulnerable group. It believes that socio-economic rights should be right-based and not otherwise, and so frowns at any interpretation of such as charity. The organisation is interested in research, development of new ideas and ways of addressing social norms in the society, promotion of education and empowerment ideas for vulnerable persons. Its greatest pride has been successes recorded at little or no cost, and the partnership it has enjoyed by friends and well wishers.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
